 # Compiled GEMM template overflows above 2^21 rows
@@ -59,7 +59,7 @@ Inferred, not measured:
 - **Workload margins against the trunk L:**
   - Rollout at 256 rows: 23.1× headroom, forward measured correct.
   - PPO minibatch at 1,024 rows: 5.78×, arithmetic only.
-  - Planned 16,384-row teacher precompute: reaches L at a mean of 256 tokens per row, so the safe mean is strictly below 256. At the probed commit `1ddc71d` the packed guard would have raised, not corrupted. Since Task 2.3 the packed path chunks at row boundaries, so a teacher chunk of this size runs in several trunk calls (CPU-tested; not measured on the GPU).
+  - Planned 16,384-row teacher precompute: reaches L at a mean of 256 tokens per row, so the safe mean is strictly below 256. At the probed commit `1ddc71d` the packed guard would have raised, not corrupted. Since Task 2.3 the packed path chunks at row boundaries, so a teacher chunk of this size runs in several trunk calls (CPU-tested). The [[model-only-sps-ceiling-bounds-per-rank-throughput|model-only SPS ceiling]] run at `e1458d2` exercised this on the GPU with a teacher proxy (`evaluate_actions` under `no_grad`, 16,384 synthetic rows, trunk compiled under the default GEMM backends): it **counted** 1, 2 and 3 trunk chunks at the sparse, mid and dense densities, as the guard predicts (`results.md`, "Flash and chunks"). That is **timing only**: no compiled-versus-eager or other numerical-correctness comparison was retained, the proxy is not the real teacher path, and the production teacher integration stays unverified.
 - **Log-ratio alarm:** treat a non-zero log-ratio at the first minibatch (before any optimizer step) as a correctness failure and abort, recording the batch shape.
 - **Upgrades:** don't upgrade torch or drivers as a remedy without a separate measured decision. Rerun both probes and the ATEN-only A/B after any upgrade; the compile-stack check rejects an unprobed torch, triton or driver until then.
 
