Independent merge verification — 2026-09-29

Reviewed HEAD `497488833aeb71b4008df408fea76e021e62d049` (`kg/merge-evidence`) against `2390c8e239a4d57770bdafd621c05abbcb326739...HEAD`. Actual parents are that base and `8093d518e439f9fae25b801b3d8545edc3631ffa`.

Finding

- P3 — `cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:62`: the current statement that 16,384-row packed chunking is “not measured on the GPU” is stale after this evidence merge. The newly added `cookbook/references/model-only-sps-ceiling-bounds-per-rank-throughput.md:38` and `pod/results_{sparse,mid,dense}.json` record 1/2/3 teacher-proxy chunks on GPU at `e1458d2`. The packed token counts are [3637248], [4194126, 770226], and [4193735, 4193735, 3228786]. Fix: credit the timing-only surrogate measurement, link the SPS Reference, and retain the unqualified numerical-correctness and real-teacher/production-integration limits. No code defect or blocking finding.

Parent preservation and resolutions

- All 141 changed paths are under `ops/` or `cookbook/`. Every application, test, config and dependency file is identical to integration base.
- All 140 incoming changed files survive: 136 are byte-identical to the incoming parent. The four differences are the documented log/index resolutions, pod FlashAttention caveat correction, and plan preserving integration's task state.
- Integration test inventory: 926 Python test function definitions and 327 Rust test functions (including ignored); no file-qualified name is lost. Incoming parent: 618 Python and 157 Rust functions. Three old Python names were already replaced on integration, with successor coverage present and passing: hidden-state/deferred-head test -> hidden-state test with implemented heads; kmax test -> enumerated trunk-GEMM width and preset checks; packed-overflow rejection -> boundary chunking, ordering/equivalence, and unfittable-row rejection. Exact mappings are in `test-successors.json`.
- All 106 integration and 57 incoming log blocks survive (block-edge whitespace normalized for comparison), no duplicate headings. Both parents' reference-index targets survive. Integration's compiled-GEMM note/index line are unchanged.
- `results.md` is byte-identical to `8093d51`, extends the exact integration prefix, and is unchanged from `9bdd82d`. Citations at lines 259–303 and 265 resolve to the expected ATEN A/B evidence.
- Corrected Task 0.3 Rust status matches its retained receipt. The pod note correctly credits the already-integrated cuBLAS-only limit revision.

