39:- **The guard, measured endpoints:** with the guard on, `_run_trunk` is correct at L−1 = 4,194,303 packed tokens. It raises at L with zero trunk calls, and chunks the padded path into calls of 4,193,735 tokens, which are also correct.
41:Inferred, not measured:
48:- **Remedy in force: cuBLAS-only compiled GEMMs.** An A/B on the same pod changed one setting, `max_autotune_gemm_backends` from `"ATEN,TRITON,CPP"` to `"ATEN"` (branch `kg/rebuild-model` at `9bdd82d`, `ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/results.md` lines 259–303; Codex r2 APPROVE).
54:- **Design bound: keep every compiled region at M × max(in, out) < 2³¹ over its Linear layers (the strict rule the guard implements; whether equality is safe on the real trunk was never measured).** This follows from the measured input-side rule plus backward: dX = dY·W reads dY at the forward output width, and weight-gradient GEMMs reduce over M. It is not justified by an output-store overflow.
56:  - Outside the trunk: the stems run eager (the full stem is 371→512→256) and have no guard of their own. Task 2.3 implements the heads and the 768-wide `actor_input_proj`; they run eager in production and chunk rows so `rows × 252 × max(3D, D, widest head) < 2^31` (11,096 rows at D = 256). Compiled, `actor_input_proj` alone would exceed L_in at 2,796,203 rows × frames. None of this is measured on the GPU.
57:- **Production compliance is unproven.** Since Task 3.1's model side, Kaggriculture is in `ModelConfig` and the model factory, and `configure_model_compile` dispatches `model_compile="trunk"` to its blocks-plus-final-norm region behind `_run_trunk`'s guard and chunking ([[kaggriculture-model-joins-isaiahs-factory-compile-and-masked-critic|Task 3.1 model-side Reference]]). That is tested on CPU with recording stand-ins only. `FullConfig` now loads it with a Kaggriculture env ([[kaggriculture-configs-follow-isaiahs-scaling-6m-recipe|configs Reference]]), but `run_ppo` stops before building an env, so full trainer integration is open. Integrated rollout, PPO recompute, evaluation, BC and teacher workloads, and real Inductor/CUDA compilation of the guarded trunk, stay unverified until the rest of Task 3.1 and Phase 6.
60:  - Rollout at 256 rows: 23.1× headroom, forward measured correct.
62:  - Planned 16,384-row teacher precompute: reaches L at a mean of 256 tokens per row, so the safe mean is strictly below 256. At the probed commit `1ddc71d` the packed guard would have raised, not corrupted. Since Task 2.3 the packed path chunks at row boundaries, so a teacher chunk of this size runs in several trunk calls (CPU-tested). The [[model-only-sps-ceiling-bounds-per-rank-throughput|model-only SPS ceiling]] run at `e1458d2` exercised this on the GPU with a teacher proxy (`evaluate_actions` under `no_grad`, 16,384 synthetic rows, trunk compiled under the default GEMM backends): it **counted** 1, 2 and 3 trunk chunks at the sparse, mid and dense densities, as the guard predicts (`results.md`, "Flash and chunks"). That is **timing only**: no compiled-versus-eager or other numerical-correctness comparison was retained, the proxy is not the real teacher path, and the production teacher integration stays unverified.
64:- **Upgrades:** don't upgrade torch or drivers as a remedy without a separate measured decision. Rerun both probes and the ATEN-only A/B after any upgrade; the compile-stack check rejects an unprobed torch, triton or driver until then.
68:- **Stack:** measured on torch 2.9.0+cu128, driver 595.91.07, RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell (sm_120). The overflow probes did not capture the installed triton (3.5.0 is the lockfile pin); the later ATEN-only A/B captured triton 3.5.0 on the same pod (`results.md` line 265).
69:- **Templates:** `mm`/`addmm` templates with fused prologues and epilogues, dynamic shapes. Unmeasured:
76:- **FlashAttention:** the overflow probe's packed-path runs used torch's ATen varlen flash shim, because that pod venv had no `flash-attn`, and its run config had `force_flash_attn: false`. The later ATEN-only A/B ran the packed trunk with real flash-attn 2.8.3 (`results.md` line 265): correct above the bound in forward under ATEN-only GEMMs. The real-trunk backward above the bound and the current wiring on a GPU remain unverified (see the [[decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only|Decision]]).
