2. Real copied Python/shell code with synthetic inputs: driver probe completeness and bench chunk/flash guards, parser/census signatures/strides/extern calls and all marker families, summary propagation, wrapper environment/CLI guards, extracted GPU-idle shell function, provenance extraction, actual manifest checks, synthetic byte comparison.
3. Actual source AST statements with mocked environment: CUDA/FlashAttention availability, forced-flash config, expected sequence length, expected compile count, observation types, import-tree checks, and mask equality. These verify preflight predicates, not CUDA dispatch.
4. Full driver/timing functions with mocked subprocesses/CUDA events: backend receipts, nonzero exit, timeout/deadline, first-failure stopping, expected-control continuation, timing statistics/counters/flash flags, and profiler device selection. These verify local decision logic, not actual GPU execution or OS process cancellation.

