+
+No r1 findings are PARTIAL or UNRESOLVED. The original r1 report was not modified; this table records its disposition.
+
+Parent preservation and conflict resolutions
+
+- All 142 three-dot changed paths are in `ops/` or `cookbook/`. Every application, test, configuration and dependency file is byte-identical to integration. Neither parent's tracked paths were deleted.
+- Of 140 paths changed on the incoming branch since the common ancestor, 136 are byte-identical to incoming. The four reconciled paths are `cookbook/log.md`, `cookbook/references/index.md`, the pod FlashAttention Reference and `ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/plan.md`. Their differences implement the stated resolutions.
+- All 1,253 integration test definitions survive: 926 Python and 327 Rust functions, including ignored tests. Incoming has 618 Python and 157 Rust definitions. Its three absent Python names were already superseded on integration: hidden-state/deferred-head rejection became hidden-state validation with implemented heads (`test_model_encoder.py:356`); the kmax check became enumeration of every trunk Linear width plus a preset check (lines 430 and 441); packed whole-batch rejection became boundary chunking, ordered/equivalent chunks and rejection of an unfittable row (lines 602, 626 and 670). The requested pytest run covers these successor tests.
+- All 106 integration log blocks and all 57 incoming blocks survive after normalizing block-edge whitespace. The five incoming unique blocks retain their newest-first order after the integration block; the two added merge/correction entries give 113 total headings, without duplicates.
+- All 19 integration and 12 incoming References index targets survive, with 21 distinct targets in HEAD. The two incoming References are at the top. The integration's compiled-GEMM account is retained, with only the explicit r1 correction in HEAD.
+- `results.md` is byte-identical to `8093d51`, extends integration's exact prefix, and is unchanged between `9bdd82d` and `8093d51`. Lines 259–303 are the ATEN A/B section; line 265 names torch 2.9.0+cu128, triton 3.5.0, flash-attn 2.8.3 and driver 595.91.07.
+- The plan's checkboxes equal integration's, and the incoming codex-exec rules survive. The two Decisions, root cookbook index and workflows index equal incoming. The Task 0.3 Rust correction matches `0.3-results.md:107–110`; the pod Reference correctly says the cuBLAS-only lane already revised the FlashAttention limit.
+
+Preservation receipts: `parent-preservation.json`, `incoming-delta-preservation.json`, `test-inventories.json`, `test-successors.json`, and `docs/preservation.json` beside this report.
+
+Fresh requested checks
+
+| Command | Result |
+| --- | --- |
+| `cargo test --manifest-path engine_rs/Cargo.toml --locked --offline` | Exit 0; 69 passed (41 + 9 + 19), no failures |
+| `cargo test` | Exit 0; 254 passed, 4 ignored, no failures |
+| `uv run python scripts/check_engine_trim.py` | Exit 0; engine trim manifest OK |
+| `uv run pytest tests/kaggriculture tests/owl tests/scripts tests/tools -m 'not slow' -q` | Exit 0; 1,673 passed, 11 skipped in 58.83 seconds; no resource guard or sharding |
+| `uv run mypy python/owl scripts` | Exit 0; no issues in 63 source files |
+
+Python skips: native grammar binding (1), CUDA pinned memory (2), trainer/run_ppo seams (4), FlashAttention/CUDA (2), quantized backend (1), native evaluation environment (1). Rust ignores: observation corpus generation and timing diagnostics (2), and expensive Orbit selected-angle audits (2). These limitations are unchanged by this evidence-only merge.
+
+Local host: macOS 26.4 arm64, Python 3.12.13, torch 2.9.0 without CUDA, rustc nightly 1.97.0 (`e9e32aca5`, 2026-04-17). The editable native module resolves to this worktree and is byte-identical to `target/debug/librs.dylib` (SHA-256 `7a7f44fae583c4ea40e4d4f2221fc8d1f69c41783a61ffb4855e5974d5816701`). No fresh maturin build was run; this is path/hash provenance, not a new build receipt. Logs and exact commands are under `checks/`; host versions are in `local-stack.json`.
+
+Documentation checks: direct cookbook shape/source lint passes on all 11 changed cookbook paths; all 39 distinct declared repository sources resolve. Docs freshness passes both the normal invocation and an explicit three-dot evaluation (zero mapped runtime-code paths). All 44 authored Markdown/Python/shell paths pass whitespace checking. The full diff flags preserved raw-output whitespace in 19 pod logs/receipts; those evidence bytes were intentionally left intact. Receipts are in `docs/` and `raw-whitespace-summary.json`.
+
+Evidence and scratch mutations
+
+- All 120 manifest entries pass the actual checksum command: ATEN A/B 69, model SPS 21, FlashAttention setup 30. For each manifest, a corrupted scratch payload failed verification and passed again after restoration.
+- The three scratch harnesses produced 96 passing records, including 79 adversarial-input or oracle positive-control cases with baseline assertions. The reviewed r1 harness was rerun from fresh HEAD copies (60 cases); two independently authored harnesses add 13 and 6 cases. These are input mutations and positive controls, not a claim that every hypothetical source-code mutant is killed.
+- Coverage includes numerical/NaN comparisons; forward, dX and parameter-gradient acceptance; complete target results; trunk calls, chunk counts and FlashAttention flags; backend start/end receipts; return codes, first-failure stopping, deadline and timeout handling; wrapper environment/CLI checks; GPU-idle predicate; source, config, shape, observation-type and mask preflights; parser/template census controls; timing arithmetic and instrumentation; transcript hash/redaction; and manifest/wheel byte-comparison controls.
+- Numerical comparators ran on CPU tensors. GPU-only preflights used actual extracted AST predicates with mocked environment. Driver subprocesses, CUDA events and profiler events were mocked. These checks test local predicates and receipt handling; they do not qualify GPU execution, live process cancellation or the production trainer.
+- Independently recomputed 560 timing samples across seven result JSONs, model-only update walls/SPS and engine budgets. `ab_summary.json` regenerates byte-identically. All ten stage backend records and four correctness stages' target coordinates agree with the frozen driver. Raw default controls contain the recorded 2/4,665 corrupt-token counts and linear illegal-memory-access result.
+- All 125 original scratch artifacts were restored byte-for-byte. Before/after hash inventory files both have SHA-256 `f8e2969edcc67e6c93f7a5a0e75980602de71111e1f9541bf93b5084ec9094ec`.
+
+Detailed coverage, limits, harnesses and logs are in `mutations/report.md` and its adjacent files. No GPU run, remote wheel/operator-transcript reread, remote pod modification or independent recount of pod-only generated caches occurred. The existing finite-loss/replay, timeline, real-trunk backward-above-bound and production-integration gaps remain explicit.
+
+Final custody
+
+SHA-256 verification confirms all 1,921 tracked files equal the starting snapshot. HEAD is unchanged; index and worktree are clean. No tracked modification was left. Receipts: `tracked-before.sha256`, `tracked-after-check.log`, `final-custody.json`.
+
+VERDICT: APPROVE

